\section{Overview}

The cosimulation infrastructure enables verification of a second C++ Berzerk
implementation against the Z80 emulator. Two levels of verification are
supported:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Subroutine-level:} Side effects (memory writes, register changes)
  at each subroutine invocation boundary must match as unordered sets.
\item \textbf{Frame-level:} VRAM content and collision flags must match at
  frame boundaries.
\end{itemize}

The system works by defining a common interface ([[BerzerkMachine]]) that both
the emulator and any second implementation must satisfy, plus data types for
capturing machine state snapshots and event logs.

