\section{Event Record Types (Phase 7.3)}

An [[EventRecord]] captures a single observable side effect within a
subroutine invocation. Events are compared as unordered sets: the C++
reimplementation may produce the same writes in a different order within
a subroutine.

Each event records both old and new values to enable bidirectional trace
debugging. The [[old\_data]]/[[old\_value]] fields are excluded from
comparison -- they exist for replay, not for verification.

<<event record types>>=
enum class EventType : uint8_t {
    MEMORY_WRITE,       // address, old_data, new_data
    IO_WRITE,           // port address, old_data, new_data
    COLLISION_CHANGE,   // intercept flag changed
};

enum class EventRegion : uint8_t {
    WORK_RAM,
    VRAM,
    COLOR_RAM,
    MAGIC_RAM,
    IO_PORT,
    OTHER,
};

struct EventRecord {
    EventType type;
    EventRegion region;
    uint16_t address;
    uint8_t old_data;
    uint8_t new_data;

    // Comparison ignores old_data (implementations may reach a subroutine
    // via different intermediate states, but must produce the same writes).
    bool operator==(const EventRecord& o) const {
        return type == o.type &&
               region == o.region &&
               address == o.address &&
               new_data == o.new_data;
    }
    bool operator!=(const EventRecord& o) const { return !(*this == o); }
};
@

\section{Machine Snapshot (Phase 7.2)}

A [[MachineSnapshot]] captures the full observable state of the machine at
a point in time. It is used for state comparison at frame boundaries and
for save/restore during debugging.

<<machine snapshot>>=
struct CpuSnapshot {
    uint16_t af, bc, de, hl;
    uint16_t af2, bc2, de2, hl2;
    uint16_t ix, iy, sp, pc, wz;
    uint8_t i, r, iff1, iff2, im;
    bool halted;

    bool operator==(const CpuSnapshot& o) const {
        return af == o.af && bc == o.bc && de == o.de && hl == o.hl &&
               af2 == o.af2 && bc2 == o.bc2 && de2 == o.de2 && hl2 == o.hl2 &&
               ix == o.ix && iy == o.iy && sp == o.sp && pc == o.pc &&
               i == o.i && r == o.r && iff1 == o.iff1 && iff2 == o.iff2 &&
               im == o.im && halted == o.halted;
    }
    bool operator!=(const CpuSnapshot& o) const { return !(*this == o); }
};

struct MachineSnapshot {
    CpuSnapshot cpu;
    std::array<uint8_t, 0x0400> work_ram;
    std::array<uint8_t, 0x2000> vram;
    std::array<uint8_t, 0x0800> color_ram;
    uint8_t magic_control;
    uint8_t magic_intercept;
    bool nmi_enabled;
    bool irq_enabled;
    int frame_number;

    bool operator==(const MachineSnapshot& o) const {
        return cpu == o.cpu &&
               work_ram == o.work_ram &&
               vram == o.vram &&
               color_ram == o.color_ram &&
               magic_control == o.magic_control &&
               magic_intercept == o.magic_intercept &&
               nmi_enabled == o.nmi_enabled &&
               irq_enabled == o.irq_enabled;
    }
    bool operator!=(const MachineSnapshot& o) const { return !(*this == o); }
};
